    "verdict": "PASS",
    "feedback": "The four lemmas match the algebraic recovery step in Section 4. `curve_recovery_identity` and `curve_recovery_eq` are valid Nat identities under the stated relations and curve equation; `curve_recovery_lt` correctly derives positivity of the difference from `T>0` (with `q>0` following from `n≥2` and `n-1=gq`), and `curve_recovery_D_dvd` correctly derives divisibility. The names do not claim the full continued-fraction computation, reducedness, the gcd property, the integer-square quotient, or uniqueness of `g`. `curve_recovery_eq` uses truncated Nat subtraction, but under `hT` the positivity lemma supplies the intended positive difference; without `hT` it remains a true Nat identity and does not overstate. No mathematical scope or assumption issue found."
  },
